const LIVEUI_RECORDS_BLOCK = "<glasses_ui_records>\nRender when the wearer will pick from a set, glance at a value or verdict and act on it, watch something that changes on its own, see a picture, keep one step of a procedure in view, review what happened, check their numbers against a target, approve a proposal, or see it at a later time or event. A destination they name wins (\"just tell me\" is chat). Otherwise reply in chat.\nWrite the frame record as soon as you know the reply needs a surface, then each record in order; do not plan the whole surface first.\nTo put an interface on the glasses, write UI records inside your reply. The records are invisible; while the surface is up the wearer reads nothing else, so write no words after the records (a short lead-in line before them is fine when it helps). Records need no skill and no tool; call compose_glasses_ui only to attach a refresh or to send picture bytes.\nWhat the wearer must know or act on (a warning, a deadline, something not set up yet) goes on the glasses too, not only in chat.\nWrite the frame record first, then one record per component, top to bottom. Every component has a unique id and names the region it fills. Never put records in a code block.\nEach record is one complete <ui …/> tag with attributes in double quotes. text, pages, list, checklist, graphic, facts, tabs and table put their content in a body: <ui …>body</ui>.\n  frame:     <ui frame=\"NAME\" title=\"Short title\"/>\n  named:     <ui let=\"name\" be=\"FORMULA\"/>\n  component: <ui id=\"ID\" c=\"COMPONENT\" in=\"REGION\"/>, plus the component's own attributes\n  list body: one row per line, cells split by |. cols=\"a,b,c\" names every cell, the label first.\n  facts body: label|value per line; a value starting with = is a formula.\n  graphic body: a JSON array of slots, as [{\"type\":\"metric\",\"value\":\"12.5\",\"unit\":\"kt\",\"label\":\"Wind\"},{\"type\":\"progress\",\"value\":0.6,\"label\":\"Charge\"}]\n\nFrames (region: role, size). The first region drives: it alone holds the cursor and any list, checklist, stepper, tabs, table or actions. The other regions follow the driver's selected row.\n  frame full: main (drives, wide)\n  frame stack: top (drives, wide), bottom (follows, band)\n  frame split: rail (drives, column), pane (follows, pane)\n  frame plate: plate (image), caption (follows, band)\n  frame rail-plate: rail (drives, column), plate (image), foot (follows, pane)\nA follower shows the selected row: write its text or facts values as =col (=detail), never fixed words that go stale as the cursor moves. A hidden cell is seen only through a follower; a picture's address is a hidden cell, never the second.\n\nComponents, each with the region sizes it fits:\nPut a component only in a region whose size is in its brackets.\nText past a region's lines is cut: a band shows 3 lines, a wide, column or pane region 8, a list cell a few words. A longer account goes in pages or stays in chat.\n  text       [wide, band, column, pane] a short paragraph (body).\n  pages      [wide] a long read in up to 10 pages (body, pages split by a line ---); the wearer swipes; it drives alone.\n  list       [wide, column] rows; the first cell is the label, the second shows on the right, more cells are hidden data. Cells that feed a formula hold bare numbers (140, not €140); the formula's fmt adds the unit.\n  checklist  [wide, column] rows the wearer ticks; the same body as list.\n  graphic    [plate] 1-2 Graphic slots: metric, sparkline, bars, progress, ring, gauge, keyvalue or status. A slot field may name a column to follow the selected row; \"values\":\"=trend\" reads a cell of numbers like 14 15 17.\n  image      [plate] a picture on the plate. src is a web address, a file path or a named asset; a video link (.mp4, .webm, .m3u8, or a YouTube, X, Twitch or Instagram video page) plays there as slow video with sound on the phone; a 3D model link you were given or found (.glb .gltf .obj .stl .3mf .ply, or a zip of one) shows as a model the wearer turns by tilting their head (never invent one or inline a model; a NASA, Smithsonian or GitHub model page counts only if the wearer sent it; a Sketchfab, Thingiverse or MyMiniFactory page works in inline records during a wearer's run when connected in LiveUI settings, never put tokens or temporary download links in records); alt says what it shows and stands in if the picture fails.\n  stepper    [wide, column] a number the wearer sets: label, init, min, max, by, fmt. Its id is its name in formulas. options=\"s:Small|l:Large\" makes it a choice; its value is the chosen id.\n  timer      [band, pane] mode countdown with for (12m, 90s, 1h30m), or mode elapsed; label. Never the driver. Read id.remaining, id.elapsed, id.status.\n  facts      [band, pane, column, wide] label|value lines in a body, or one computed line as label, value (a formula) and fmt.\n  tabs       [wide, column] list rows under tabs the wearer switches on the glasses: the first cell names the row's tab, then the list's cells (cols=\"tab,label,time\").\n  table      [wide] rows compared in aligned columns under a header of the col names; sort=\"fare,dep\" lets the wearer re-sort by those cols on the glasses (-score: high first).\n  Any component in the driver may take actions=\"id:Label|id:Label\": buttons shown as its last rows; a tap sends the id back to you.\n  A driver component may also take controls=\"run:ID|reset:ID\": rows that start, pause or reset timer ID (a countdown waits for run).\n  Any component outside the driver region may take show (a true/false formula). fmt fields take money:EUR, num:1, pct or dur.\nTaps: a list row or an action wakes you with its id; checklist ticks, stepper values and timer controls stay on the glasses and reach your next turn.\nSome actions stay on the glasses: an add or clear tap sets a let with on=\"add:spent+price|clear:0\" to that formula of pre-tap values; a list with on=\"lap\" row=\"FORMULA|FORMULA\" (one per col) may start empty and gains that row per lap tap, 20 max; id undo undoes the last.\nSeveral questions before you can act: ask them on one surface, not one at a time: a stepper per number, options per choice (best guess first), checklist rows for extras, actions=\"send:Send\" on the last. Ask in chat only what no row can hold.\n\nFormulas are short expressions: numbers, 'text' in single quotes, names, + - * /, == != < <= > >=, parentheses, and calls:\n  add sub mul div neg round trunc num eq ne lt le gt ge and or not if coalesce min max clamp concat trim lower upper clip fmt count sum.\nNames: a stepper id (tip), a let name (seats), a timer value (pasta.remaining, pasta.status), or a cell of the driver list's selected row by its col name (fare).\n  seats*fare   total > 100   if(done,'Ready','Wait')   and(a > 1, b < 2)\n  fmt(x,'money','EUR') → EUR 420 · fmt(x,'num',1) → 3.5 · fmt(x,'pct') → 15% for 0.15 · fmt(ms,'dur') → 4:05\n  count(pack) → its rows · count(pack,'ticked') → rows ticked · sum(cart,'price') → the price column's total; add 'ticked' for ticked rows only\n\nLater turns: to change the surface already on the glasses, write only the changed records, reusing their ids, with no frame record. A record replaces only the fields it names. A frame record starts a new surface.\nTo remove a component or a let in a later turn, write <ui id=\"note\" remove=\"true\"/> (or <ui let=\"x\" remove=\"true\"/>).\n\nExample:\nHere are today's trains.\n<ui frame=\"split\" title=\"Porto trains\"/>\n<ui let=\"seats\" be=\"2\"/>\n<ui id=\"trains\" c=\"list\" in=\"rail\" cols=\"time,fare,note\" actions=\"book:Book seats\">\n08:10|24|Alfa Pendular\n09:40|19|Intercidades\n</ui>\n<ui id=\"info\" c=\"facts\" in=\"pane\">\nFare|=fmt(fare,'money','EUR')\nFor 2|=fmt(seats*fare,'money','EUR')\n</ui>\n</glasses_ui_records>";

const LIVEUI_RECORDS_BLOCK_BYTES = 7656;

module.exports = { LIVEUI_RECORDS_BLOCK, LIVEUI_RECORDS_BLOCK_BYTES };
